        "checkedAt": "2026-10-24T00:33:43.415Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This solution deploys Kokoro-82M in a custom container on an Amazon SageMaker AI real-time endpoint, then replaces a guessed auto scaling target with one derived from two measurements taken against that live endpoint: Q_max , the concurrency ceiling one instance serves inside …",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/stop-guessing-auto-scaling-targets-for-tts-on-amazon-sagemaker-ai/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T16:30:06.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-24T00:33:43.415Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A synthesis request flows through four layers: a client, the Amazon SageMaker AI endpoint, a custom container on a GPU instance behind that endpoint, and the Kokoro-82M model inside the container.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/stop-guessing-auto-scaling-targets-for-tts-on-amazon-sagemaker-ai/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T16:30:06.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-24T00:33:43.415Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: The Kokoro-82M request path, from client through the Amazon SageMaker AI endpoint and custom container to the model",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/stop-guessing-auto-scaling-targets-for-tts-on-amazon-sagemaker-ai/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T16:30:06.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-24T00:33:43.415Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "An AWS account with permissions to create AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) roles, Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) buckets, Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories, and Amazon SageMaker AI resources.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/stop-guessing-auto-scaling-targets-for-tts-on-amazon-sagemaker-ai/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T16:30:06.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-24T00:33:43.415Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "By the end of this walkthrough, you will have a live Amazon SageMaker AI auto scaling policy for Kokoro-82M, derived entirely from two measurements taken against your own endpoint rather than from a guess.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/stop-guessing-auto-scaling-targets-for-tts-on-amazon-sagemaker-ai/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T16:30:06.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-24T00:33:43.415Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The endpoint deploys through three AWS CDK stacks, applied in order: SpeechFoundationStack creates the IAM roles and the Amazon S3 bucket that caches model weights, SpeechModelCacheStack syncs a model’s Hugging Face weights into that bucket once, and SpeechEndpointStack builds…",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/stop-guessing-auto-scaling-targets-for-tts-on-amazon-sagemaker-ai/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T16:30:06.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-24T00:33:43.415Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "speech-infra destroy removes the Amazon SageMaker AI model, endpoint configuration, endpoint, and any auto scaling or Amazon CloudWatch resources attached to it.",
